{风格}
Image 1 is a layout sketch. The tan blocks mark the cabinetry (tall units on both sides, upper cabinets above, plinth and floor below) and the dark quadrilateral in the middle is an empty built-in refrigerator niche. Follow the exact position, size and perspective of every block, so the whole cabinet wall shares one consistent perspective. The dark niche must stay exactly where it is, with the same shape and size, as an empty dark recess with nothing inside: no refrigerator, no doors, no objects. Do not make the niche taller, wider or deeper than drawn. Its edges sit flush with the cabinet fronts and its bottom edge meets the floor line of the cabinets. {参考图说明}
To the left of the niche the cabinetry opens into a small everyday coffee counter: upper cabinets, an open recess with a honed pale limestone worktop and backsplash, and base cabinets below. {摆件} Nothing overlaps the niche. Finely textured limewash wall, pale oak plank floor.
{光线}
Oak grain with natural variation, restrained stone veining, matte surfaces with subtle real-world imperfections. Natural architectural perspective with straight verticals, no ultra-wide distortion. Crisp but not over-sharpened, very fine film grain that does not hide detail. Not a 3D render, no plastic look, no heavy HDR, no repeating textures.
No text, letters, numbers, logos, arrows, labels or watermarks anywhere.
